const HALLOWEEN_2025_TURN_HINTS={"galvantula":["Set Sunny Day and Tailwind before Fire attacks. Galvantula can paralyze the team at 100% HP.","At 75%, Light Screen appears: use physical Fire attacks for this turn.","Use Defog twice to remove Light Screen and Sticky Web. Raw damage is not a substitute.","Resume Fire attacks after clearing the screens and hazards.","P1 renews Tailwind to maintain speed advantage.","Final wave of Fire attacks; check the boss's remaining resistances."],"banette":["P1 uses Sunny Day / Incinerate to consume the boss's Sitrus Berry, followed by three Flamethrowers.","Four Flamethrower users are needed; the source does not prescribe exact Pokémon for each slot.","Continue special Fire attacks; Cotton Guard boosts the boss's physical Defense.","Four Flamethrowers remain scheduled despite Calm Mind at 50%.","Use four Flamethrowers and watch the move-lock effect near 20%.","Finish with Flamethrower, using distinct species and held items per team member."],"hypno":["P1 sets Sunny Day and Safeguard, P2 Defog removes Reflect, P3/P4 use Flare Blitz.","P1–P3 use Sucker Punch; P4 uses Trick Room to counter the opponent's Trick Room.","All players use Sucker Punch. The source recommends resetting if the add is Tyranitar.","Four Flare Blitz attacks after the priority-move phase.","The type chart reverses near 33% HP; follow the listed Fighting-type attacks.","All four players continue with Fighting-type moves."],"golurk":["P1 sets Rain Dance and Tailwind; P2 removes Stealth Rock with Defog; P3/P4 use Water attacks.","Four Water attacks in rain. Avoid Rock/Steel/Dark targets that might draw healing Drain Punch.","Water attacks continue; watch for changes to rain and the boss healing with Drain Punch.","Keep using Water moves as the boss boosts every stat near 60%.","P3 refreshes Tailwind; other players continue Water attacks.","Final Water-type attack sequence."],"scolipede":["P1 sets sun and Incinerate against Sitrus Berry; P2 sets Tailwind; P3/P4 use Fire moves.","Prioritize special Fire attacks against the +2 Defense boost at 75%.","P1 uses Haze to remove the boss boosts while the others use Fire moves.","All four players use Fire attacks after the stat reset.","P3 renews Tailwind and P4 uses Haze; P1/P2 attack with Fire moves.","Four Fire attacks; Speed Boost can make timing crucial."],"mandibuzz":["P1 uses Rain Dance and Tailwind; P2/P3/P4 use Thunder. Violent winds may force switches.","Use four Thunder attacks; rain makes Thunder more reliable.","P2 uses Haze without Prankster to cancel Nasty Plot; the others use Thunder.","All players use Thunder while monitoring forced switches.","P3 renews Tailwind, P4 uses non-Prankster Haze, P1/P2 use Thunder.","Finish with four Thunders, adjusting for forced Pokémon replacements."],"absol":["P1 sets Tailwind while P2/P3/P4 use Fighting-type attacks.","All players attack with Fighting moves; random 'bad luck' events may interfere.","Continue Fighting attacks while watching Thunder Wave and Swords Dance.","P1 uses Heal Block before the boss's Wish heals it; others attack with Fighting moves.","P2 renews Tailwind; three players use Fighting attacks.","Final sequence uses Fighting moves, subject to random effects."],"darkrai":["Lead with Chesto Berry or Vital Spirit against Dark Void. P4 sets Tailwind.","Four Close Combat attacks; maintain the rotation before type inversions.","Use Close Combat or Sacred Sword, depending on the caav guide version.","Four Close Combats, keeping spare Pokémon for the type-chart reversal.","P1 uses Tailwind, P2/P3 use fast Close Combat, P4 uses Psycho Cut at the correct Speed.","After type inversion, all players switch to Psycho Cut."]};
